Statement of changes (Apache License 2.0, Section 4b)
-----------------------------------------------------

The following changes have been made to the original HyperFrames work:

1. Renamed throughout, from HyperFrames to SmashCut. This covers the npm scope
   (@hyperframes/* -> @smashcut/*), the CLI binary, package and skill names,
   documentation, and the runtime identifier prefixes (hf-* -> sc-*,
   __hf* -> __sc*).

   Deliberately NOT renamed, because they refer to a third party rather than to
   this project:
     - HeyGen as a service provider: the `heygen` CLI, api.heygen.com and other
       heygen.com endpoints, HEYGEN_* environment variables, and the
       X-HeyGen-Client-Source request header. These are calls into HeyGen's
       platform and renaming them would break voice, music and asset retrieval.
     - References to the upstream project's own URLs and repository
       (hyperframes.heygen.com, heygen-com/hyperframes), which are retained as
       accurate attribution.

2. Removed HeyGen's brand marks. The `hyperframes-logo-*` image assets were
   deleted rather than renamed, and replaced with SmashCut's own wordmark.
   Apache-2.0 Section 6 grants no trademark rights, so redistributing those
   marks under this project's name would be a misuse of them regardless of the
   code licence.

3. Added application capture. SmashCut adds the ability to drive a real
   application — a web app, a locally running app, or a command-line program —
   through a scripted and asserted flow, record it, and hand the resulting
   footage and shot manifest to the composition pipeline. This capability does
   not exist in the original work.

The LICENSE file and CREDITS.md are retained from the original work, unmodified.
